{
  "id": 22,
  "name": "isolation_spread_hybrid",
  "intent": "Add a spread penalty to discourage boundary picks between clusters, complementing the parent's isolation ratio. Spread is the std of candidate-to-unvisited distances; low spread indicates a dense local neighborhood (good for cluster absorption), high spread indicates a boundary position (often suboptimal). Cluster_density weight is modestly boosted (0.05->0.08) to address the clustered family where the parent loss was highest at 0.0514. The combined cluster signals (cd + isolation + spread-penalty) target the worst-performing family while preserving early-tour outlier absorption for uniform instances.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "local_distance"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    r = f['return_distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    mr = f['mean_remaining']\n    g = f['regret']\n    p = f['progress']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    sp = f['spread']\n    inv_mr = 1.0 / max(mr, 1e-9)\n    isolation = 1.0 - nr * inv_mr\n    return -d + (0.15 + 0.45 * p) * r + (0.35 - 0.15 * p) * g + 0.08 * (1 - p) * cd + 0.10 * (1 - p) * isolation - 0.08 * sp",
  "source": "live_llm",
